# SABOTAGE: R10's period gate is dropped from every posting action — the database belt is left holding the door alone.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 3 (ADR-054 D7) gates every action that lands a POSTED row with
# `Samen.Scopes.Finance.PeriodGuard`: `:post`, `:void`, and `:create_reversal`
# (the posted-born factory AP approval, the stock-receipt bridge, the sales
# bridge and VoidGuard all ride). This patch keeps all three actions' other
# guards — PostBalance, DimensionBalance, PostGuard, VoidGuard — and removes ONLY
# the three `PeriodGuard` changes.
#
# That is the plausible regression, not a strawman: the migration's trigger also
# refuses a posted row dated inside a CLOSED period, so a reviewer who reads only
# the belt concludes the Ash gate is redundant and deletes it. What the belt
# cannot do is tell a DOCUMENT from a journal-only adjustment, so SOFT-CLOSE
# stops meaning anything: a supplier bill posts straight into a soft-closed month
# while the close is still being prepared. And on a mount where the belt is off
# (a restored database, a trigger disabled during an incident, the samen_web
# subset mount) a closed period stops refusing anything at all.
#
# Why the flip is attributable: the raw-SQL belt legs stay GREEN under this patch
# (the trigger is untouched), as do the one-way close transition, the read-mirror
# anti-tautology leg and every control. Only the two Ash-layer legs red — which is
# what says the flip landed on the period gate rather than on the belt, the
# schema or the test file.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_periods_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a SOFT-CLOSED period refuses a DOCUMENT post
# MUST_FAIL: with the period trigger DISABLED, the closed-period post is still refused
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/blueprint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/blueprint.ex
@@ -313,8 +313,7 @@
             require_atomic?(false)
             # R10 (WS-ACCT Phase 3): the posting's DATE must land in a period
             # that still admits it — a closed period refuses always.
-            change({Samen.Scopes.Finance.PeriodGuard, period: unquote(period_mod)})
             change(Samen.Scopes.Finance.PostBalance)
             # R6 over the PERSISTED lines (PostBalance's twin): the stored rows,
             # never a caller argument, decide whether the posting balances per
             # cost object.
@@ -330,6 +329,5 @@
             require_atomic?(false)
             # R10: the reversal is dated the ORIGINAL's date, so a closed period
             # would refuse it mid-action — refuse up front, naming the period.
-            change({Samen.Scopes.Finance.PeriodGuard, period: unquote(period_mod)})
             change(Samen.Scopes.Finance.PostBalance)
             change(Samen.Scopes.Finance.PostGuard)
@@ -371,6 +369,5 @@
             # R10 (WS-ACCT Phase 3): this is the posted-born factory every
             # DOCUMENT posting rides (AP approval, the stock-receipt bridge, the
             # sales bridge, a void's reversal), so one gate here covers them all.
-            change({Samen.Scopes.Finance.PeriodGuard, period: unquote(period_mod)})
             change(Samen.Scopes.Finance.PostGuard)
           end
